  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 6847779261494379404, guid: cf59afdc9e0ffee49924ebb9a0a10e75, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning home after picking up yarn from the market.
    - Resident returning to the southern apartment block.
    - Visiting a neighbor to help hem some new curtains.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Seeking shelter from the heavy smog in the district.
    - Checking on the status of the local communal kitchen.
    - Seeking refuge from the radioactive dust storms.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Returning to assigned bunk for the final lockdown.
    - Seeking refuge from the falling black ash.
    - Fulfilling mandatory elderly residency check-in.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Going to the theater for a 10:00 PM opera.
    - Picking up a pension check from a bank that closed in 1960.
    - Buying fresh strawberries in the middle of a blizzard.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Returning to a house that was condemned for radiation.
    - Meeting a sister who passed away during the Great Frost.
    - Taking a walk in the park while the chemical sirens are active.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Going home to plant flowers in the radioactive ash.
    - I need to go buy more silk for a wedding dress.
    - To wait for the sun to come out from behind the smoke.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Hello, dear. You look thin; are they feeding you enough at this booth?
    - Here are my papers. I kept them under my Bible so they wouldn't wrinkle.
    - "It\u2019s a bit chilly today. I hope you\u2019re wearing your thermal vest
      under that uniform."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - There is a small tear in your sleeve, dear. Bring it here, I have my needle.
    - "The sky looks so bruised lately. I think I\u2019ll go home and make some soup."
    - My hands are shaking a bit more today. The air has a very metallic taste.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019m going home to finish a sweater for my grandson. It\u2019s a very
      bright red."
    - "Don't worry about the sirens, dear. It\u2019s just the world having a little
      tantrum."
    - "Everything is going to be fine once I finish the mending. You\u2019ll see."
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - 
    - 
