    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Bless you, dear. Stay warm and don't work too hard.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Go home soon. The air isn't good for young lungs like yours.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "I\u2019ll save a bowl of soup for you. Be safe in the quiet."
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Oh, am I staying here? Well, at least it gives me time to knit.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Is the heater working in there? My bones get so cold these days.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - A nice quiet room. I can finally finish my stitching in peace.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - "Oh... I think... I\u2019ve dropped... my thimble..."
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - "My... threads... they\u2019re all... getting tangled..."
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - "It\u2019s okay... the world... was getting... too heavy... anyway..."
  quarantineExitLines:
  - Oh, a rest? Well, I suppose my feet could use one.
  - "Will you send word to Irina? She worries when I don\u2019t come home on time."
  - "I\u2019ll just sit and knit. That\u2019s what I do. That\u2019s what I\u2019ve
    always done."
  killExitLines:
  - "Oh\u2026 I must have\u2026 dropped a stitch\u2026 somewhere\u2026"
  - "I never did finish that sweater\u2026 I had the red wool\u2026 right here\u2026"
  - "Don\u2019t you fuss, dear\u2026 It\u2019s alright\u2026 I\u2019ve been ready\u2026
    for a while\u2026"
